# Copy to .env (gitignored). `alchemy deploy` and `alchemy plan` load it. See docs/deploy.md.

# Custom domain (SITE_DOMAIN_<STAGE>), once the zone is in the Cloudflare account.
# Unset = workers.dev URL only.
# SITE_DOMAIN_PROD=example.com

# Hostname for the one sprites bucket (game icons), served straight from R2 through Cloudflare's
# cache. Prod's deploy creates the bucket and attaches it. Unset = prod's Worker serves them at
# /sprites/<key> (a Worker request per icon).
# SPRITES_DOMAIN=sprites.example.com

# Hostname for the stage's renders bucket (RENDERS_DOMAIN_<STAGE>), served the same way. With either
# domain set, prod's deploy also manages the zone's cache rules (docs/deploy.md, "Edge cache").
# Unset = the Worker serves render images at /prints/<id>/render/<file>.
# RENDERS_DOMAIN_PROD=renders.example.com

# Uploading renders to the deployed renders bucket (`bun run render --upload prod`; docs/deploy.md,
# "Uploading renders"): an R2 API token with Object Read & Write on that bucket only. The account
# comes from CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID (below) or the only account `wrangler whoami` lists.
# R2_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# The daily views rollup Worker and `bun run views:sync` (docs/deploy.md, "Page views"): an API token
# with Account Analytics: Read only, for the Analytics Engine SQL API. The deploy binds it to the
# Worker as a secret. Not CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN, which would replace your login.
# ANALYTICS_API_TOKEN=

# Rendering (`bun run render`, and starting batches from /admin/render under `bun run dev`): the
# fpsr sprite assets built from an installed Factorio, and the mirror clone the panel renders from
# (default ~/data/factorio-mirror).
# FPSR_ASSETS_DIR=/path/to/fpsr/assets-out/<game version>
# RENDER_CLONE_DIR=/path/to/factorio-mirror
# Where renders are written and read (default data/renders in the repo). A full set is hundreds of
# GB in millions of files, which editors and other tools would try to index, so keep it outside the
# repo. Every run must use the same folder: its files are what tell a run a page needs no redraw.
# RENDERS_DIR=~/data/factorio-renders

# /admin (Cloudflare Access; docs/deploy.md, "Admin page"). The Zero Trust team domain, and the
# one email address allowed into /admin. Unset = /admin is a 404.
# ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=<team>.cloudflareaccess.com
# ADMIN_EMAIL=you@example.com

# Opt out of Alchemy's anonymous CLI telemetry.
# ALCHEMY_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1

# CI only (a GitHub Action has no browser login). On your own machines use
# `bun alchemy profile edit --add Cloudflare` instead, and never commit a token.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
# CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=
